n (the hundred-millions place) and write down 0 in the ten-millions place:.\n\n```.\n  0 + 6 + 1 (carried over) = 7.\n```.\n\nFinally, we have 7 in the hundred-millions place, so we don't need to carry over anything further.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum of 693046763 and 499017855 is:.\n\n```.\n  693046763.\n+ 499017855.\n---------.\n1192064618.\n```.\n\nSo, the sum is 1192064618.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
