messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 940833598 and 885048752? Please reason step by step.', "<think>.\nTo find the sum of 940833598 and 885048752, we can follow these steps:.\n\n1. Align the numbers by their place values, making sure that the ones, tens, hundreds, thousands, and so on, are in the same columns.\n2. Add the digits in each column, starting from the rightmost column (the ones place).\n3. If the sum of the digits in any column is 10 or more, carry over the extra digit to the next column to the left.\n4. Continue adding the digits in each column, including any carried-over digits, until you reach the leftmost column (the millions place).\n\nLet's perform the addition:.\n\n```.\n  940833598.\n+ 885048752.\n-----------.\n```.\n\nStarting from the rightmost column (the ones place):.\n\n```.\n  8 + 2 = 10 (write down 0 and carry over 1).\n```.\n\nNext column (the tens place):.\n\n```.\n  9 + 7 + 1 (carried over) = 17 (write down 7 and carry over 1).\n```.\n\nNext column (the hundreds place):.\n\n```.\n  3 + 8 + 1 (carried over) = 12 (write down 2 and carry over 1).\n```.\n\nNext column (the thousands place):.\n\n```.\n  3 + 5 + 1 (carried over) = 9.\n```.\n\nNext column (the ten-thousands place):.\n\n```.\n  8 + 4 + 1 (carried over) = 13 (write down 3 and carry over 1).\n```.\n\nNext column (the hundred-thousands place):.\n\n```.\n  0 + 5 + 1 (carried over) = 6.\n```.\n\nNext column (the millions place):.\n\n```.\n  4 + 8 + 1 (carried over) = 13 (write down 3 and carry over 1).\n```.\n\nNext column (the ten-millions place):.\n\n```.\n  0 + 8 + 1 (carried over) = 9.\n```.\n\nFinally, the leftmost column (the hundred-millions place):.\n\n```.\n  9 + 0 = 9.\n```.\n\nPutting it all together, we get:.\n\n```.\n  940833598.\n+ 885048752.\n-----------.\n  1825882350.\n```.\n\nSo, the sum of 940833598 and 885048752 is 1825882350.\n</think>.\n<answer>. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
